PREFACE

  Regulation 3 of 2006

  Regulation establishing a common customs tariff for the Hesperian Union

  Regulation of the Assembly of the Hesperian Union and of the Hesperian Council establishing a common customs tariff and laying down the rates of duty applicable to goods imported into the customs territory of the Union from third countries.

PREAMBLE

  Having regard to the Treaty establishing the Hesperian Union, and in particular Article 27 thereof,

  Having regard to the proposal from the Hesperian Commission,

  Having regard to the opinion of the Union Economic and Social Committee,

  Whereas:

  (1) The establishment of the internal market requires the adoption of a common customs tariff applicable to the external frontiers of the Union so as to ensure equal conditions of competition and equal protection of producers across all member states.

  (2) The nomenclature of the common customs tariff should follow the international Harmonised System established by the World Customs Organisation, adapted to the particular requirements of the Union.

  (3) Preferential rates of duty should be accorded to goods originating in countries with which the Union has concluded association or trade agreements.

  THE ASSEMBLY OF THE HESPERIAN UNION AND THE HESPERIAN COUNCIL, Having regard to the Treaty establishing the Hesperian Union, HAS ADOPTED THIS REGULATION:

BODY

CHAPTER 1 - GENERAL PROVISIONS

  ARTICLE 1 - Subject matter

    This Regulation establishes a common customs tariff for the Hesperian Union and lays down the nomenclature, rates of duty and rules of origin applicable to goods imported from third countries.

  ARTICLE 2 - Scope

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The common customs tariff shall apply to the importation of goods into the customs territory of the Union from any country or territory not forming part of that territory.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      Goods in free circulation within the Union shall not be subject to the duties laid down in this Regulation when they are moved from one member state to another.

  ARTICLE 3 - Tariff schedule

    The rates of conventional duty applicable to goods imported into the Union are set out in the following schedule:

