  ARTICLE 4 - Rules of origin

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      Goods shall be deemed to originate in the country in which they were wholly obtained or in which they underwent the last substantial transformation.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The Commission shall adopt delegated acts laying down detailed rules for the determination of origin.

CHAPTER 2 - TARIFF ADMINISTRATION

  ARTICLE 5 - Amendment of the schedule

    PARAGRAPH (1)

      The Commission may, by delegated act, amend the rates set out in the schedule in Article 3 to give effect to trade agreements concluded by the Union.

    PARAGRAPH (2)

      The Commission shall publish the amended schedule in the Official Journal.

  ARTICLE 6 - Entry into force

    This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the Hesperian Union.
